<title>ITALY: Italian inflation slows to 18-year low.</title>
<headline>Italian inflation slows to 18-year low.</headline>
<dateline>ROME</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy's consumer price index slipped to an 18-year low last month, the National Statistics Office reported Tuesday.</p>
<p>It said the key measure of inflation fell to an annual rate of 2.4 percent in February from 2.6 percent in January, the lowest CPI inflation rate in Italy since May 1969.</p>
